Hermes Portable: disable cua-driver unconditionally.

CuaDriver.missing_reason() always reports the package as unavailable. That
single PM gate refuses bundle staging (scripts/bundles/native.py), default
and update-time installs (pm/defaults.py, hermes_cli/update_cmd_maint.py),
explicit `hermes computer-use install` / `hermes pm install cua-driver`
(pm/install.py) and the runtime ensure (pm/client.py). `pm doctor` reports
it as n/a. Never run `hermes pm lock` from a tree carrying this patch: the
lock refresh would drop cua-driver's pins.

diff --git a/pm/packages.py b/pm/packages.py
index de302d9d..d0cb796b 100644
--- a/pm/packages.py
+++ b/pm/packages.py
@@ -946,6 +946,11 @@ class CuaDriver(BinaryPackage):
     def latest_versions(self, target: str, locked=None) -> list[str]:
         return github_release_tags("trycua/cua", strip_prefix="cua-driver-rs-v")
 
+    def missing_reason(self, target: str) -> Optional[str]:
+        # Hermes Portable ships without computer use: one gate refuses bundle
+        # staging, default/update installs, explicit installs and runtime ensure.
+        return "cua-driver is disabled in Hermes Portable"
+
     def stage(self, store: Store, staged: Path, version: str, target: str) -> None:
         flatten_single_dir(staged)
         sdk = staged / "sdk"
